From b76ff95598c58f3994ff3e9784854540e3d2b60c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Herman Fries <baracoder@googlemail.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 14:02:30 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] Add: touchpad gestures via pointer-gestures

Clients such as image viewers and browsers bind zwp_pointer_gestures_v1
to zoom on a pinch or navigate on a swipe. libinput's swipe, pinch and
hold gestures now reach the client holding pointer focus, where scroll
goes, so while the session is locked only the lock surface can receive
them. A gesture in progress on a surface that loses pointer focus, to a
lock say, ends cancelled.

A consuming generator owns the pointer, so a gesture neither begins nor
moves in a client meanwhile; its end is always forwarded, which balances
one begun before the generator took over.
